  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Behavior",
  "description": "The meme implicitly references the stereotype that Black women are 'too hot' or 'too dark' to be on the beach, which is a form of racialized behavior stereotype. The text 'i don't like the sun so i wear a visor' is a pun that plays on the idea that Black women are 'too hot' to be on the beach, which is a form of racialized behavior stereotype.",
